<title>JAPAN: Japan June imported vehicles down 20.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June imported vehicles down 20.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of imported vehicles in Japan fell 20.5 percent in June from a year earlier to 32,176 units, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>It was the third successive month that sales had fallen on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>Japan's imported vehicle sales in the first six months of calendar 1997 totalled 194,741 units, down 8.7 percent from the same period last year, the association said.</p>
<p>The June breakdown of vehicle imports, with percentage changes from a year earlier, was as follows:</p>
<p> Cars total		30,536  down 17.5 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc   19,846  down 25.8 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  10,690  up    4.1 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total	     1,639  down 52.6 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy		    1,496  down 27.2 percent</p>
<p> - Light			143  down 89.8 percent</p>
<p> Buses			  one  versus six</p>
<p>Exporting countries and selected makers' car sales in Japan in June, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> German total		   15,420  down 14.1 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group	5,491  up   10.4 percent</p>
<p>  -Volkswagen		    4,625  up   15.4 percent</p>
<p>  -Audi				866  down 10.4 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel			2,892  down 31.8 percent</p>
<p>  BMW				3,172  down 20.3 percent</p>
<p>  Mercedes-Benz		  3,262  down 17.3 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG		    301  down 49.4 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche			    275  up   32.9 percent</p>
<p> United States total	   7,396  down 31.9 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA			2,367  down 44.3 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor			 609  down 63.0 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors		 2,035  up   20.0 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota			     306  down 81.0 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler			 1,506  up    6.7 percent</p>
<p>  Saturn				74  vs nil</p>
<p>  BMW USA			    382  vs nil</p>
<p> Britain total		   3,270  up    3.6 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		    2,860  down  0.8 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			     211  down  3.2 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     142  vs    nil</p>
<p> Sweden total		    2,232  down 15.6 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo			    2,213  down 13.3 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				  19  down 79.3 percent</p>
<p> France total			826  down  8.6 percent</p>
<p>  Peugeot Citroen		  691  up   10.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Peugeot			  488  up   47.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Citroen			  203  down 30.2 percent</p>
<p>  Renault			    135  down 52.0 percent</p>
<p> Italy total			 894  up   40.8 percent</p>
