<p> Spain total			 180  down 72.6 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     180  down 72.6 percent</p>
<p> Netherlands			 201  vs  nil</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			 201  vs  nil</p>
<p> Australia			    49  down 66.4 percent</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			  49  down 66.4 percent</p>
<p>Note: General Motors' June car sales included 1,236 Cavaliers sold by Toyota, up 83.7 percent from a year earlier. The June total included 60 Nissan AD vans made in Mexico, down from 1,340 the year before.</p>
<p>Saturn refers to cars sold through the Saturn division of General Motors. BMW USA figure refers to the Z3 two-seater convertible sports car made by BMW's U.S. unit.</p>
<p>Of the total, sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers totalled 3,430 in June, down 58.3 percent from a year earlier, bringing the figure for the January-June period to 27,809 units, down 43.2 percent from the same period of 1996.</p>
